), N6 (terminal), or N1 → N7 (terminal). All lead to terminal. So from N8, opponent wins immediately. So if you go to N3, you give opponent a winning move from N8. So this is bad.  \n- N2 → N3 or N4. From N3, opponent gets to N8 → again, opponent wins. From N4 → terminal. So opponent can win from N4. So from N2, opponent can win either way. So N2 is losing.  \n\nThus, moving to N4 leads to a terminal win for the player who moves to N5 — a winning move. So best move is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.3263440860215055, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N4, N3, or N2. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position.  \n- N4 → N5 (terminal): immediate win for the player who moves to N5. So, the next player loses. So, moving to N4 results in opponent's loss — a win.  \n- N3 → N8 → (N9, N6, N1). From N8, opponent can go to N9 (terminal), N6 (terminal), or N1 → N7 (terminal). All lead to terminal. So from N8, opponent wins immediately. So if you go to N3, you give opponent a winning move from N8. So this is bad.  \n- N2 → N3 or N4. From N3, opponent gets to N8 → again, opponent wins. From N4 → terminal. So opponent can win from N4. So from N2, opponent can win either way. So N2 is losing.  \n\nThus, moving to N4 leads to a terminal win for the player who moves to N5 — a winning move. So best move is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N6, N1\nN4 -> N5\nN0 -> N4, N3, 