egal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N0, N9\nN6 -> N7, N9, N3\nN7 -> N2\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0, N5, N4\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> N8\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N9, the only legal move is to N8. N8 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N8 is the only option and results in an immediate win for the current player. Therefore, N8 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4931239388794567, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the only legal move is to N8. N8 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N8 is the only option and results in an immediate win for the current player. Therefore, N8 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}]
