 to N13, N1, and N7.  \n- N13 leads to N8, N3, N0, N9: all of which eventually reach terminal nodes. N13 is a move into a branch that may be losing if the opponent plays well.  \n- N1 leads to N5 → N2 or N7. N5 can go to N2 → N13 or N7 → N4 → N11. These paths can be deep and lead to a long game with strategic value.  \n- N7 leads to N4 → N11 (terminal) or N12 (terminal), both immediate terminal. This is a safe win for the player making the move.  \n\nBut crucially, **N7 leads directly to a terminal state**, meaning the player who moves to N7 immediately ends the game and wins (since opponent has no move). Hence, choosing N7 ends the game immediately and wins. Therefore, N7 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.2983305036785513, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N13, N1, and N7.  \n- N13 leads to N8, N3, N0, N9: all of which eventually reach terminal nodes. N13 is a move into a branch that may be losing if the opponent plays well.  \n- N1 leads to N5 → N2 or N7. N5 can go to N2 → N13 or N7 → N4 → N11. These paths can be deep and lead to a long game with strategic value.  \n- N7 leads to N4 → N11 (terminal) or N12 (terminal), both immediate terminal. This is a safe win for the player making the move.  \n\nBut crucially, **N7 leads directly to a terminal state**, meaning the player who moves to N7 immediately ends the game and wins (since opponent has no move). Hence, choosing N7 ends the game immediately and wins. Therefore, N7 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format 