[2026-08-12 13:50:22] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N11\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN12 -> N6, N10\nN3 -> terminal\nN13 -> N3, N8\nN7 -> N1, N5\nN11 -> N9, N4\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N13, N12\nN10 -> N7, N6\nN8 -> N2, N3\nN4 -> N0, N5\n\nLegal moves: N9, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N11, the legal moves are to N9 and N4. N4 leads directly to N0 or N5, both terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately since the opponent has no further moves. Thus, moving to N4 ends the game immediately and wins. Therefore, N4 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5085738539898133, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N11, the legal moves are to N9 and N4. N4 leads directly to N0 or N5, both terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately since the opponent has no further moves. Thus, moving to N4 ends the game immediately and wins. Therefore, N4 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN12 -> N6, N10\nN3 -> terminal\nN13 -> N3, N8\nN7 -> N1, N5\nN11 -> N9, N4\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N13, N12\nN10 -> N7, N6\nN8 -> N2, N3\nN4 -> N0, N5\n\nLegal moves: N0, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N0 and N5. Both N0 and N5 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, either choice ends the game on the next turn with a win. Since both result in an immediate win for the current player, either is equally optimal. Choosing either is valid; we select one. N5 is chosen as it appears earlier in the list.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 0.46765704584040746, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N0 and N5. Both N0 and N5 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, either choice ends the game on the next turn with a win. Since both result in an immediate win for the current player, either is equally optimal. Choosing either is valid; we select one. N5 is chosen as it appears earlier in the list.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N4\nN0 -> N5, N1\nN9 -> N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N8\nN6 -> N2, N0\nN7 -> N6, N5\n\nLegal moves: N9, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9 and N8. N9 leads to N7, then to N6 or N5; both N6 and N5 eventually lead to terminal nodes via branching. N8 leads to N9 or N4. N4 and N5 lead directly to terminal nodes. However, from deeper analysis, N8 has access to a loop path (N8 → N9 → N7 → N6 → N0 → N5 → terminal), and the game state becomes critical due to reachability. Since every path from N3 to terminal is finite, the player who starts at N3 and chooses N8 or N9 can avoid immediate terminal, but due to symmetry and forced entry into a chain ending in terminal nodes (no cycles), it's a zero-sum impartial game. The player forcing entry into terminal nodes after even number of moves wins. N3 → N8 is a strong move because it leads to a longer chain, giving more control. Ultimately, choosing N8 allows control of the game path and avoids early loss. Therefore, optimal play is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6426994906621393, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9 and N8. N9 leads to N7, then to N6 or N5; both N6 and N5 eventually lead to terminal nodes via branching. N8 leads to N9 or N4. N4 and N5 lead directly to terminal nodes. However, from deeper analysis, N8 has access to a loop path (N8 → N9 → N7 → N6 → N0 → N5 → terminal), and the game state becomes critical due to reachability. Since every path from N3 to terminal is finite, the player who starts at N3 and chooses N8 or N9 can avoid immediate terminal, but due to symmetry and forced entry into a chain ending in terminal nodes (no cycles), it's a zero-sum impartial game. The player forcing entry into terminal nodes after even number of moves wins. N3 → N8 is a strong move because it leads to a longer chain, giving more control. Ultimately, choosing N8 allows control of the game path and avoids early loss. Therefore, optimal play is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move l