 terminal or lose. The critical choice is to reach a forcing position to end the game on a terminal edge. Going to N1 allows us to continue, and from N4, we can reach terminal after opponent’s turn. Therefore, going from N9 to N1 leads to forced win by ensuring opponent loses next. The best outcome is to go to N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 0.36918505942275043, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the only legal move is to N1. From N1, the player can go to N4 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal, so the opponent has no move and wins immediately if we go to N6. But going to N4 allows continuation. From N4, the next move is to N0 or N8, both terminal. Thus, any continuation leads to terminal. The game will reduce to terminal after moves. Since we control the path, choosing to go from N9 to N1 is the only choice, and from N1, the player who moves to N4 leads to a sequence of moves where the opponent will eventually face terminal or lose. The critical choice is to reach a forcing position to end the game on a terminal edge. Going to N1 allows us to continue, and from N4, we can reach terminal after opponent’s turn. Therefore, going from N9 to N1 leads to forced win by ensuring opponent loses next. The best outcome is to go to N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}]
