[2026-08-12 13:57:05] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN13 -> terminal\nN11 -> N0\nN7 -> N6, N1\nN9 -> N13\nN8 -> N13, N3\nN6 -> N2, N9\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2\nN10 -> N12\nN1 -> N8, N5\nN12 -> terminal\nN4 -> N10, N11\nN2 -> terminal\nN0 -> N10, N7\n\nLegal moves: N10, N11assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N10 and N11.  \n- N10 leads to N12 (terminal) → immediate win for the player who moves to N10 (since the opponent has no move after).  \n- N11 leads to N0, then from N0 possible moves: N10 or N7. N10 again leads directly to terminal, and N7 continues to N6 or N1. But all chains eventually lead to terminal via backtracking and reach a leaf.  \nBut crucially, N10 is a direct terminal win (after N10 → N12 terminal). So playing to N10 ends game immediately and wins.  \nThus, choosing N10 is best — it maximizes the chance of immediate terminal and thus victory. Therefore, N10 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6028013582342955, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N10 and N11.  \n- N10 leads to N12 (terminal) → immediate win for the player who moves to N10 (since the opponent has no move after).  \n- N11 leads to N0, then from N0 possible moves: N10 or N7. N10 again leads directly to terminal, and N7 continues to N6 or N1. But all chains eventually lead to terminal via backtracking and reach a leaf.  \nBut crucially, N10 is a direct terminal win (after N10