y go to terminal) → again, the opponent can play, and from those, all paths reach terminal.  \nEventually every path from N12 leads to opponent taking control of a terminal edge and winning.  \nThus N8 leads to immediate terminal and player wins. N12 leads to opponent to always have options until end and thus lose. Therefore, choosing N8 ensures victory.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N1, N10\nN11 -> N7, N10\nN2 -> N5, N4\nN8 -> N4, N3\nN0 -> N11, N1\nN13 -> N8, N12\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N9\nN12 -> N2, N6\nN9 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N4 and N3. Both N4 and N3 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, either move results in an immediate win. Either choice is optimal; however, since both are equally beneficial, selecting either is fine. We choose N4 as a valid maximizing move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4803904923599321, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N4 and N3. Both N4 and N3 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, either move results in an immediate win. Either choice is optimal; however, since both are equally beneficial, selecting either is fine. We choose N4 as a valid maximizing move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"