ove. Therefore, the optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N9, N7\nN9 -> N1\nN6 -> N3, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0, N5\nN7 -> N8, N9\nN5 -> N6, N0\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 or N7.  \n- Moving to N9: Then path goes N9 → N1 (terminal). The opponent has no move and wins. So we lose.\n- Moving to N7: Then path goes N7 → N8 or N7 → N9.\n    - From N8: N8 → N0 (terminal) or N8 → N5.\n        - If N8 → N0, opponent's turn ends immediately, so they lose, and we win.\n        - If N8 → N5, N5 → N6 → (then N6 → N3 or N2), both go to terminal. So again, opponent loses.\n    - From N7 → N9: leads to N1 terminal — opponent loses immediately.\nSo from N7: both branches lead to opponent losing eventually — thus optimal choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 1.3912563667232598, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 or N7.  \n- Moving to N9: Then path goes N9 → N1 (terminal). The opponent has no move and wins. So we lose.\n- Moving to N7: Then path goes N7 → N8 or N7 → N9.\n    - From N8: N8 → N0 (terminal) or N8 → N5.\n        - If N8 → N0, opponent's turn ends immediately, so they lose, and we win.\n        - If N8 → N5, N5 → N6 → (then N6 → N3 or N2), both go to terminal. So again, opponent loses.\n    - From N7 → N9: leads to N1 terminal — opponent loses immediately.\nSo from N7: both branches lead to oppone