[2026-08-12 14:07:31] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN14 -> N11\nN0 -> N9\nN10 -> N14, N5\nN6 -> N0\nN11 -> terminal\nN1 -> N14, N6\nN17 -> N6, N4\nN7 -> N8\nN15 -> terminal\nN3 -> N17, N4\nN13 -> N16, N12\nN8 -> N1, N3\nN4 -> N15, N13\nN16 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N10\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N7 and N10. Analyzing each path:  \n- Move to N7: from N7 you go to N8; from N8 you have N1 or N3. N8→N3 leads to N4→N15 or N13. If N4 goes to N13→N16 terminal, or N4 to N15 terminal. Either way, the opponent wins unless you block terminal earlier.  \n- Move to N10: N10 → N14 → N11 → terminal. So opponent loses immediately.  \nClearly, N10 leads to terminal directly in a short path after a move, thus winning immediately. Thus, move to N10 is optimal. The outcome of N7 leads to a longer game and opponent gains edge, but N10 gives a win. Thus, choosing N10 is better.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6146859083191851, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N7 and N10. Analyzing each path:  \n- Move to N7: from N7 you go to N8; from N8 you have N1 or N3. N8→N3 leads to N4→N15 or N13. If N4 goes to N13→N16 terminal, or N4 to N15 terminal. Either way, the opponent wins unless you block terminal earlier.  \n- Move to N10: N10 → N14 → N11 → terminal. So opponent loses immediately.  \nClearly, N10 leads to terminal directly in a short path after a move, thus winning immediately. Thus, move to N10 is optimal. The outcome of N7 leads to a longer game and opponent gains edge, but N10 gives a win. Thus, choosing N10 is better.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N10\n\nDirected graph:\nN14 -> N11\nN0 -> N9\nN10 -> N14, N5\nN6 -> N0\nN11 -> terminal\nN1 -> N14, N6\nN17 -> N6, N4\nN7 -> N8\nN15 -> terminal\nN3 -> N17, N4\nN13 -> N16, N12\nN8 -> N1, N3\nN4 -> N15, N13\nN16 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N10\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N14, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N10, the legal moves are to N14 and N5. N5 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4973684210526317, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N10, the legal moves are to N14 and N5. N5 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N2, N7\nN8 -> N5, N3, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7, N6\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9\nN9 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1\nN3 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N5, N3, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N5, N3, or N6. We analyze each choice:  \n- To N5: Then the next state is N5 → from which the opponent faces N5 → N7 or N6. N5 → N7 leads to terminal, so opponent wins. N5 → N6 leads to N6 → N9 → terminal. But from N6, the player at the turn will eventually win since terminal comes after. So if player reaches N5, then the opponent can win by going from N5 to N7 or N6.  \n- To N3: From N3 → N0 → the opponent has full choice from N0 to N4, N2, N7. But N2 and N7 are terminal paths: if opponent chooses N2 or N7 (directly), then you will lose. N0 → N4 → N1 → terminal. So all such routes end, thus opponent can control.  \n- To N6: Then N6 → N9 → terminal → you win immediately since next player can't act, thus this move leads to immediate loss for opponent, thus a winning move.\n\nHence, N6 leads to a terminal state on the next turn for the opponent; thus, this is the optimal move. So the best outcome from N8 is going to N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.3560554612337296, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N5, N3, or N6. We analyze each choice:  \n- To N5: Then the next state is N5 → from which the opponent faces N5 → N7 or N6. N5 → N7 leads to terminal, so opponent wins. N5 → N6 leads to N6 → N9 → terminal. But from N6, the player at the turn will eventually win since terminal comes after. So if player reaches N5, then the opponent can win by going from N5 to N7 or N6.  \n- To N3: From N3 → N0 → the opponent has full choice from N0 to N4, N2, N7. But N2 and N7 are terminal paths: if opponent chooses N2 or N7 (directly), then you will lose. N0 → N4 → N1 → terminal. So all such routes end, thus opponent can control.  \n- To N6: Then N6 → N9 → terminal → you win immediately since next player can't act, thus this move leads to immediate loss for opponent, thus a winning move.\n\nHence, N6 leads to a terminal state on the next turn for the opponent; thus, this is the optimal move. So the best outcome from N8 is going to N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N2, N7\nN8 -> N5, N3, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7, N6\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9\nN9 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1\nN3 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N9, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N9 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N9 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4939728353140917, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N9, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N9 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N9 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that