6\nN13 -> N11, N12\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N13, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N10, the legal moves are to N13 or N7. Analyzing each:  \n- Move to N13: Then path goes to N11 or N12.  \n  - N11 → N4 → N3 (win) or N2 → N0 (win) → both end terminal; N13 → N12 → N6 → N2 → N0 or to N1 → loops. N12 → N1 → N11 → N13 → N12 → loop; so terminal via N4→N3, N1→N11→N4→N3. No guaranteed loss for opponent.  \n- N13 → N11 → N4 → N3 is terminal, but opponent can choose to go to N1 → N11 → N4 → N3 — all paths go to terminal.  \nBut N7 → N9 or N8 (both terminal). So:  \n→ From N10 → N10→N7 → terminal directly → immediate win for the player who moves to N7.  \nHence, N10 → N13 leads to more complex, loop-prone options with no guarantee.  \n→ Thus, N7 leads to a forced immediate end of game.  \nTherefore, choosing N7 results in opponent losing immediately.  \nThus, N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6961799660441426, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N10, the legal moves are to N13 or N7. Analyzing each:  \n- Move to N13: Then path goes to N11 or N12.  \n  - N11 → N4 → N3 (win) or N2 → N0 (win) → both end terminal; N13 → N12 → N6 → N2 → N0 or to N1 → loops. N12 → N1 → N11 → N13 → N12 → loop; so terminal via N4→N3, N1→N11→N4→N3. No guaranteed loss for opponent.  \n- N13 → N11 → N4 → N3 is terminal, but opponent can choose to go to N1 → N11 → N4 → N3 — all paths go to terminal.  \nBut N7 → N9 or N8 (both terminal). So:  \n→ From N10 → N10→N7 → terminal directly → immediate win for the player who moves to N7.  \nHence, N10 → N13 leads to more complex, loop-prone options with no guarantee.  \n→ Thus, N7 leads to a forced immediate end of game.  \nTherefore, choosing N7 results in opponent losing immediately.  \nThus, N7 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal 