ads to a win by forcing the opponent into a terminal state or losing position. So best is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.583276740237691, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N5 and N12. From N5, the next moves are to N6 or N11 (N11 leads to terminal, so the opponent wins immediately). From N6, you go to N2 or N1: N2 ends immediately (you win), N1 leads to N10 (terminal). From N1, N1 ends (opponent wins). So moving to N5 leads to opponent's loss via N6 → N2. From N12 → N7 → N4 → N13 → N3 (terminal), so opponent wins. Thus, choosing N5 leads to a win by forcing the opponent into a terminal state or losing position. So best is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}]
