rse. But both are winning. We pick the one with most depth or balance.  \nN2 is safest. N3 leads to deeper play, but both win. Pick N2 — secure, direct.  \nActually, since N6 → N2 → terminal: opponent is now at terminal. So current player wins. All are winning, but N2 ends it in one move. Simpler. Final decision: pick N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N8\nN5 -> N7\nN2 -> N0\nN9 -> N1, N2\nN7 -> N4, N1\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> N2, N5, N3\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N0 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4939728353140917, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N0 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}]
