ze each destination to determine the best outcome, i.e., the one that leads to a forced win or minimizes the opponent's options.  \n- Move to N8: leads to N8→N5 or N8→N2. N5→N9 (terminal) or N2→terminal. But N5 can be forced to terminal quickly. The path N1→N8→N5→N9 or N8→N2 both terminate the game immediately after one move to terminal. So the opponent wins if the game starts with a forced exit.  \n- Move to N4: then N→N6→N11 or N6→N10. N→N6→N10→N12 ends terminal. N→N6→N11→N7→N3 or N7→N13 (both terminals). Both paths eventually end.  \n- Move to N5: leads directly to N5→N9 (terminal). This gives opponent no choice — they lose immediately. So this move wins immediately.  \nThus, going to N5 is optimal since it ends the game in one move, forcing the opponent to lose. This is a win for the current player.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.3484153933220148, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N1, the legal moves are to N8, N4, or N5. We analyze each destination to determine the best outcome, i.e., the one that leads to a forced win or minimizes the opponent's options.  \n- Move to N8: leads to N8→N5 or N8→N2. N5→N9 (terminal) or N2→terminal. But N5 can be forced to terminal quickly. The path N1→N8→N5→N9 or N8→N2 both terminate the game immediately after one move to terminal. So the opponent wins if the game starts with a forced exit.  \n- Move to N4: then N→N6→N11 or N6→N10. N→N6→N10→N12 ends terminal. N→N6→N11→N7→N3 or N7→N13 (both terminals). Both paths eventually end.  \n- Move to N5: leads directly to N5→N9 (terminal). This gives opponent no choice — they lose immediately. So this move wins immediately.  \nThus, going to N5 is optimal since it ends the game in one move, forcing the opponent to lose. This is a win for the current player.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose o