or opponent. Therefore, N7 maximizes winning chance.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N4, N8, N6\nN6 -> N3, N1\nN9 -> N0\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2\nN1 -> N9\nN5 -> N6, N1, N7\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N8, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N4, N8, or N6. N4 and N8 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N4 or N8 ends the game on the next turn for the opponent, resulting in an immediate win. Therefore, choosing N4 or N8 is optimal. Between them, both end the game immediately, so either is equally good. However, N8 leads directly to terminal with no further play, making it a simpler, certain win. Thus, N8 is chosen as it is a winning move with no risk.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 1.1012167515563103, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N4, N8, or N6. N4 and N8 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N4 or N8 ends the game on the next turn for the opponent, resulting in an immediate win. Therefore, choosing N4 or N8 is optimal. Between them, both end the game immediately, so either is equally good. However, N8 leads directly to terminal with no further play, making it a simpler, certain win. Thus, N8 is chosen as it is a winning move with no risk.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt