s best.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.3670911148839842, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N0, N3, or N5. We analyze each destination:  \n- If we move to N0: then to N7 (by the next player), who can go to N4 or N9. Then, if N5 → N4 is the key, the game may lead to N7 → N4 → N8 (terminal), or N7 → N9 (terminal). So either way, terminal is reached from N4 or N9. So, the player who moves the token to terminal loses. This means if we can force the opponent to reach a terminal from a terminal node or to move from terminal, the outcome is critical.  \n- N3 leads to N1 or N2 both are terminal nodes (direct terminal) so the opponent will be on terminal. The opponent will lose.  \n- N5 → N7 → N0 or N4, then to terminal. N5 → N7 → N9 (terminal) or N4 → N8 (terminal).  \nThe best option is moving to N3: the opponent will have to move into a node that ends in terminal directly or lose. N3 → N2 or N1 leads to terminal. So opponent has no valid move from N3 after any next move, so they will lose immediately.  \nThus, choosing N3 leads to immediate loss for opponent (win for me). N3 is best.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}]
