inue, and you win.\n\nThus, moving to N7 ensures immediate terminality for opponent. This choice wins.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.3314374646293153, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N0, N2, or N7. We need to determine which of these leads to a winning position. Since the player who cannot move loses, a node that leads to terminal nodes for the opponent is desirable. We analyze each choice:\n\n- Move to N0: leads to N1 from the graph, then the opponent has choices. N1 → N8 (terminal), N5 → terminal. So the opponent wins if they move correctly. This is a losing path for us.\n\n- Move to N2: leads to N7 or N0. N7 → N6 (terminal), N6 → terminal, and N3 → N4 → terminal. N7 is a winning move for opponent. N0 leads to N1, which can lead to terminal paths. So the opponent will win.\n\n- Move to N7: leads to N6 (terminal) or N3. N6 ends game immediately (opponent to move fails). N3 → N4 → terminal. Thus, both paths result in terminal states for the opponent. So from N7, opponent cannot continue, and you win.\n\nThus, moving to N7 ensures immediate terminality for opponent. This choice wins.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8, N5\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> N4\nN2 -> N7, N0\nN7 -> N6, N3\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N2, N7\n\nLegal moves: N6, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N6 and N3. N6 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediatel