[2026-08-12 14:32:24] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N8, N4\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N4\nN7 -> N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5, N6\nN0 -> N7, N1\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5 and N6.  \n- Moving to N5 gives the opponent access to N9 or N0.  \n  - From N9: moves to N0 or N4 (N4 leads to terminal, so losing on N4).  \n  - From N0: move to N7 or N1, N7 leads to N2 (terminal), N1 leads to terminal. So, N0 is losing.  \n  - From N9 and N0, opponent will win.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N8 or N4. Both N8 and N4 go to terminal, so the opponent has no move from these.  \nSo, the player who moves to N6 ends the game (opponent loses). Thus, N6 leads to a winning outcome.  \nThus, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6036502546689304, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5 and N6.  \n- Moving to N5 gives the opponent access to N9 or N0.  \n  - From N9: moves to N0 or N4 (N4 leads to terminal, so losing on N4).  \n  - From N0: move to N7 or N1, N7 leads to N2 (terminal), N1 leads to terminal. So, N0 is losing.  \n  - From N9 and N0, opponent will win.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N8 or N4. Both N8 and N4 go to terminal, so the opponent has no move from these.  \nSo, the player who moves to N6 ends the game (opponent loses). Thus, N6 leads to a winning outcome.  \nThus, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N8, N4\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N4\nN7 -> N2\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5, N6\nN0 -> N7, N1\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N8 and N4. N8 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N8 is a winning move. N4 also leads to terminal, so it's also a losing move for the opponent. However, since moving to N8 ends the game immediately with a win, it is optimal. Therefore, the best choice is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.46765704584040746, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N8 and N4. N8 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N8 is a winning move. N4 also leads to terminal, so it's also a losing move for the opponent. However, since moving to N8 ends the game immediately with a win, it is optimal. Therefore, the best choice is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything e