[2026-08-12 14:33:41] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> N6, N9\nN8 -> N2, N1\nN3 -> N8, N4\nN0 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6, N3\nN6 -> N2\nN4 -> N5, N0\n\nLegal moves: N6, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N6 or N3.  \n- If we move to N6, the next move is to N2, and the game ends because N2 leads to terminal. So the opponent has no move and loses. Thus, we win.  \n- If we move to N3, the opponent can go to N8, which leads to N2 or N1 both terminal. But if they go to N8, opponent wins. Alternatively, if they go to N3 → N8 → N1 or N2 (terminal). So opponent can win.  \nThus, going to N6 gives us a win. So, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5705432937181665, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N6 or N3.  \n- If we move to N6, the next move is to N2, and the game ends because N2 leads to terminal. So the opponent has no move and loses. Thus, we win.  \n- If we move to N3, the opponent can go to N8, which leads to N2 or N1 both terminal. But if they go to N8, opponent wins. Alternatively, if they go to N3 → N8 → N1 or N2 (terminal). So opponent can win.  \nThus, going to N6 gives us a win. So, choosing N6 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no l