oses immediately.  \nBest outcome: choosing N8 immediately wins the game because opponent has no move. So N8 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> terminal\nN1 -> N9, N12, N13\nN12 -> N2, N6\nN3 -> N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N11, N5, N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN11 -> N1\nN13 -> N12, N10\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> N4\nN9 -> N3\nN5 -> N11, N3\n\nLegal moves: N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, the only legal move is to N4. N4 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N4 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4939728353140917, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, the only legal move is to N4. N4 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N4 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}]
