rs alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N4, N3\nN8 -> N9, N7\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0, N1\nN0 -> N6, N4\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N8\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5\n\nLegal moves: N0, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N0 or N1.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N3, which ends at terminal, so player to move loses. So the player who moves to N1 will lose.  \n- Moving to N0 gives the opponent a choice from N0 → N6/N4.  \n- N6 → N9 or N8 → terminal or N9. N8 → N9 → terminal, N4 → N5 → terminal.  \nSo, N0 leads to terminal paths eventually, so the opponent eventually loses if they play optimally.  \nThus, moving to N0 wins.  \nHence, best move is to N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4286078098471986, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N0 or N1.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N3, which ends at terminal, so player to move loses. So the player who moves to N1 will lose.  \n- Moving to N0 gives the opponent a choice from N0 → N6/N4.  \n- N6 → N9 or N8 → terminal or N9. N8 → N9 → terminal, N4 → N5 → terminal.  \nSo, N0 leads to terminal paths eventually, so the opponent eventually loses if they play optimally.  \nThus, moving to N0 wins.  \nHence, best move is to N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\