[2026-08-12 14:44:13] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N1, N3\nN5 -> N2, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN0 -> N5, N1\nN1 -> N8, N9\nN9 -> N7, N8\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N4\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N5 or N1.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N2 (terminal), or N6.  \n  - From N6, the options are to N1 or N3.  \n    - N3 leads to terminal.  \n    - N1 leads to N8 or N9.  \n      - N8 leads to N4 (terminal).  \n      - N9 leads to N7 (terminal) or N8 (then terminal).  \n  - So from N5, the opponent is forced into terminal.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N8 or N9.  \n  - Both N8 and N9 lead to terminal paths eventually.  \n  So, moving to N5 leads to a win.  \nThus, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5934634974533106, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N5 or N1.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N2 (terminal), or N6.  \n  - From N6, the options are to N1 or N3.  \n    - N3 leads to terminal.  \n    - N1 leads to N8 or N9.  \n      - N8 leads to N4 (terminal).  \n      - N9 leads to N7 (terminal) or N8 (then terminal).  \n  - So from N5, the opponent is forced into terminal.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N8 or N9.  \n  - Both N8 and N9 lead to terminal paths eventually.  \n  So, moving to N5 leads to a win.  \nThus, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N1, N3\nN5 -> N2, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN0 -> N5, N1\nN1 -> N8, N9\nN9 -> N7, N8\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N4\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N2 and N6. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4999151103565365, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N2 and N6. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN9 -> N8, N0\nN1 -> N6, N4\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N2, N3\nN0 -> N1, N2\n\nLegal moves: N9, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9 or N0.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - N8 leads to N2 (terminal or to N3 → N7 terminal) or N3 → N7 terminal.  \n  - N0 leads to N1 or N2 (both eventually to terminal).  \n  - So from N9, the opponent can eventually be forced to a terminal move.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N1 or N2.  \n  - N1 → N6 or N4 (both terminal).  \n  - N2 → terminal.  \n  So, moving to N0 ends the game on opponent's move.  \nThus, choosing N9 gives the opponent a better chance to win.  \nChoosing N0 ensures a terminal node immediately (for the opponent).  \nTherefore, to maximize outcome (win), choose N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6112903225806452, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9 or N0.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - N8 leads to N2 (terminal or to N3 → N7 terminal) or N3 → N7 terminal.  \n  - N0 leads to N1 or N2 (both eventually to terminal).  \n  - So from N9, the opponent can eventually be forced to a terminal move.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N1 or N2.  \n  - N1 → N6 or N4 (both terminal).  \n  - N2 → terminal.  \n  So, moving to N0 ends the game on opponent's move.  \nThus, choosing N9 gives the opponent a better chance to win.  \nChoosing N0 ensures a terminal node immediately (for the opponent).  \nTherefore, to maximize outcome (win), choose N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN9 -> N8, N0\nN1 -> N6, N4\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N2, N3\nN0 -> N1, N2\n\nLegal moves: N1, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N1 and N2. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N1 and N2. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N1, N13\nN12 -> N7, N3\nN0 -> N12, N3\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2, N8\nN10 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N10, N0\nN1 -> N11, N5\nN11 -> N9, N10\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN13 -> N6, N7\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N1, N13assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N1 or N13.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N11 or N5.  \n  - N5 leads to N2 (terminal), N8.  \n    - N8 leads to N10 (terminal) or N0.  \n    - N0 leads to N12 or N3 (both terminal).  \n    - N12 leads to N7 (terminal).  \n  - N11 leads to N9 or N10 (both terminal).  \n  Thus, from N1 all paths eventually end with a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N13 leads to N6 or N7.  \n  Both N6 and N7 are terminal.  \n  \nSo from N4:  \n- Move to N1 gives opponent to play first from a complex graph eventually leading to terminal,  \n- Move to N13 leads immediately to terminal.  \nBut wait: player who moves to N13, then the opponent gets to move from N6 or N7 (both terminal) — so the player who just moved to N13 has forced the opponent to face no legal moves. Thus, by choosing N13, the player wins.  \n\nHence, choosing N13 is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6775042444821733, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N1 or N13.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N11 or N5.  \n  - N5 leads to N2 (terminal), N8.  \n    - N8 leads to N10 (terminal) or N0.  \n    - N0 leads to N12 or N3 (both terminal).  \n    - N12 leads to N7 (terminal).  \n  - N11 leads to N9 or N10 (both terminal).  \n  Thus, from N1 all paths eventually end with a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N13 leads to N6 or N7.  \n  Both N6 and N7 are terminal.  \n  \nSo from N4:  \n- Move to N1 gives opponent to play first from a complex graph eventually leading to terminal,  \n- Move to N13 leads immediately to terminal.  \nBut wait: player who moves to N13, then the opponent gets to move from N6 or N7 (both terminal) — so the player who just moved to N13 has forced the opponent to face no legal moves. Thus, by choosing N13, the player wins.  \n\nHence, choosing N13 is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N13\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N1, N13\nN12 -> N7, N3\nN0 -> N12, N3\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2, N8\nN10 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N10, N0\nN1 -> N11, N5\nN11 -> N9, N10\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN13 -> N6, N7\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N6, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N13, the legal moves are to N6 and N7. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N6 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.49906621392190154, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N13, the legal moves are to N6 and N7. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N6 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N4, N8, N5, N11\nN4 -> N5\nN1 -> N11\nN3 -> N12\nN12 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N13, N2\nN6 -> N9, N4, N3\nN2 -> N1, N7\nN8 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> N10\nN11 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N4, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N9, N4, or N3.  \n- N9 leads to N4, N8, N5, N11 (N8 and N11 are terminal, so N4 and N5 continue).  \n- N4 leads to N5 (then to N0, N13, N2).  \n- N3 leads to N12 (terminal).  \n\nBut N4 leads to N5 which leads to N0 → N10 (terminal), N13 (terminal), or N2 → N1 → N11 (terminal), N7 (terminal). So N5 leads to a terminal state.  \n\nThe game ends on any terminal node. So the player who forces the move into a terminal is the one who wins, assuming opponent plays randomly.  \nN3 leads immediately to terminal (N12).  \nThus, choosing N3 wins immediately.  \nSo the optimal move is to go directly to N12.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.2923882286361065, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N9, N4, or N3.  \n- N9 leads to N4, N8, N5, N11 (N8 and N11 are terminal, so N4 and N5 continue).  \n- N4 leads to N5 (then to N0, N13, N2).  \n- N3 leads to N12 (terminal).  \n\nBut N4 leads to N5 which leads to N0 → N10 (terminal), N13 (terminal), or N2 → N1 → N11 (terminal), N7 (terminal). So N5 leads to a terminal state.  \n\nThe game ends on any terminal node. So the player who forces the move into a terminal is the one who wins, assuming opponent plays randomly.  \nN3 leads immediately to terminal (N12).  \nThus, choosing N3 wins immediately.  \nSo the optimal move is to go directly to N12.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N4, N8, N5, N11\nN4 -> N5\nN1 -> N11\nN3 -> N12\nN12 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N13, N2\nN6 -> N9, N4, N3\nN2 -> N1, N7\nN8 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> N10\nN11 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N12assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the only legal move is to N12, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N12 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N12 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N12</answer>", "episode_score": 0.49057724957555177, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the only legal move is to N12, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N12 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N12 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N12</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N14\n\nDirected graph:\nN17 -> N11, N6\nN0 -> terminal\nN13 -> N4, N7\nN6 -> N13, N15\nN9 -> N12\nN11 -> N5, N3\nN7 -> N4\nN3 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN14 -> N8, N2\nN1 -> N17, N6\nN15 -> N16\nN16 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN2 -> N9, N0\nN5 -> N10\nN8 -> N17, N1\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N14, the legal moves are to N8 and N2.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N17 (to N11 or N6), or N1.  \n- From N1: moves to N17 or N6.  \n- N1 → N6 → N13 → N4 or N7 → N4 (terminal or N5 → N10 (terminal).  \n- N6 → N13 → N4 or N7 → N4 (terminal).  \n- N17 → N11 → N5 or N3 (N3 → terminal), or N5 → N10 → terminal.  \nSo paths from N8 lead to terminal states, the opponent eventually wins.  \n\nMoving to N2:  \n- N2 → N9 → N12 → terminal or N0 → terminal.  \nEither way, the opponent loses immediately, as both are terminal nodes.  \nThus, choosing N2 leads to the opponent having no move (winning the game).  \nThus, choosing N2 is the best move.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6410016977928692, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N14, the legal moves are to N8 and N2.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N17 (to N11 or N6), or N1.  \n- From N1: moves to N17 or N6.  \n- N1 → N6 → N13 → N4 or N7 → N4 (terminal or N5 → N10 (terminal).  \n- N6 → N13 → N4 or N7 → N4 (terminal).  \n- N17