[2026-08-12 14:45:20] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7\nN2 -> N8, N4\nN3 -> N5, N1\nN8 -> N0, N6\nN4 -> N9, N6\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N3, N7\n\nLegal moves: N8, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N8 and N4.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N0 or N6.  \n  - N0 → terminal (win for the opponent).  \n  - N6 → N7 (terminal).  \n  So from N8, the opponent wins immediately from N0 or N7.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N9 or N6.  \n  - N9 → N3 → N5 (terminal) or N1 (terminal).  \n  - N6 → N7 (terminal).  \n  So from N4, all paths lead to terminal.  \n  \nThus, moving to N4 leads to terminal no matter what the opponent does. The opponent has no legal moves and loses.  \nTherefore, choosing N4 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4073853989813243, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N8 and N4.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N0 or N6.  \n  - N0 → terminal (win for the opponent).  \n  - N6 → N7 (terminal).  \n  So from N8, the opponent wins immediately from N0 or N7.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N9 or N6.  \n  - N9 → N3 → N5 (terminal) or N1 (terminal).  \n  - N6 → N7 (terminal).  \n  So from N4, all paths lead to terminal.  \n  \nThus, moving to N4 leads to terminal no matter what the opponent does. The opponent has no legal moves and loses.  \nTherefore, choosing N4 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7\nN2 -> N8, N4\nN3 -> N5, N1\nN8 -> N0, N6\nN4 -> N9, N6\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N3, N7\n\nLegal moves: N9, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 and N6. N6 leads to N7, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N6 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4956706281833616, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 and N6. N6 leads to N7, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N6 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7\nN2 -> N8, N4\nN3 -> N5, N1\nN8 -> N0, N6\nN4 -> N9, N6\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N3, N7\n\nLegal moves: N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N7, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N7 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N7 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4939728353140917, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N7, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N7 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N7 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8\nN3 -> N7, N1\nN5 -> N3, N0\nN0 -> N9, N4\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N7\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N3 and N0.  \n- Moving to N3: Then the path continues to N7 or N1.  \n  - N7 → N8 → terminal (win for the opponent if it’s the next move)  \n  - N1 → N2 or N8 (N2 → N6 or N7).  \n  - Both N6 and N7 lead to terminal, so opponent wins if player can force a terminal.  \n  - However, N2 → N7 (then N8 → terminal).  \n- Moving to N0: Then path continues to N9 or N4, both terminal.  \n  So if I move to N0, opponent is forced to a terminal node and I win.  \nThus, moving to N0 leads to a win.  \nTherefore, choosing N0 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6036502546689304, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N3 and N0.  \n- Moving to N3: Then the path continues to N7 or N1.  \n  - N7 → N8 → terminal (win for the opponent if it’s the next move)  \n  - N1 → N2 or N8 (N2 → N6 or N7).  \n  - Both N6 and N7 lead to terminal, so opponent wins if player can force a terminal.  \n  - However, N2 → N7 (then N8 → terminal).  \n- Moving to N0: Then path continues to N9 or N4, both terminal.  \n  So if I move to N0, opponent is forced to a terminal node and I win.  \nThus, moving to N0 leads to a win.  \nTherefore, choosing N0 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> N12, N1\nN10 -> N13, N4\nN3 -> N5, N7\nN4 -> N13, N0\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6, N9\nN11 -> terminal\nN2 -> N11, N10\nN5 -> N2, N8\nN13 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N1\n\nLegal moves: N5, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5 and N7.  \n- Moving to N5: the next node is N5 → N2 or N8.  \n  - N8 leads to terminal → win.  \n  - N2 → N11 (terminal) or N10 → N13 (terminal) or N4 → N13 or N0 (terminal). All paths eventually lead to terminal.  \n  - So, the player who moves to N5 wins if they force the opponent into a losing position.  \n- Moving to N7: the next node is N7 → N6 or N9  \n  - N6 → N0 (terminal) or N1 (terminal)  \n  - N9 → N12 (terminal) or N1 → terminal.  \n  - All moves from N7 also end in terminal.  \n- However, N5 leads to N8 which is a terminal move — so the player to move from N5 can immediately win.  \nThus, moving to N5 allows the current player to win immediately if the opponent has no choice.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6528862478777588, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5 and N7.  \n- Moving to N5: the next node is N5 → N2 or N8.  \n  - N8 leads to terminal → win.  \n  - N2 → N11 (terminal) or N10 → N13 (terminal) or N4 → N13 or N0 (terminal). All paths eventually lead to terminal.  \n  - So, the player who moves to N5 wins if they force the opponent into a losing position.  \n- Moving to N7: the next node is N7 → N6 or N9  \n  - N6 → N0 (terminal) or N1 (terminal)  \n  - N9 → N12 (terminal) or N1 → terminal.  \n  - All moves from N7 also end in terminal.  \n- However, N5 leads to N8 which is a terminal move — so the player to move from N5 can immediately win.  \nThus, moving to N5 allows the current player to win immediately if the opponent has no choice.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8\nN3 -> N7, N1\nN5 -> N3, N0\nN0 -> N9, N4\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N7\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N9 and N4. N9 and N4 both lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves end the game on the next turn. Since the player to move wins if the opponent has no move, choosing either N9 or N4 results in an immediate win. Both are winning moves, but since the goal is to maximize the outcome (i.e., win), either is optimal. However, as both lead to victory, either choice is equally good. Still, choosing N4 is sufficient and direct.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4404923599320883, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N9 and N4. N9 and N4 both lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves end the game on the next turn. Since the player to move wins if the opponent has no move, choosing either N9 or N4 results in an immediate win. Both are winning moves, but since the goal is to maximize the outcome (i.e., win), either is optimal. However, as both lead to victory, either choice is equally good. Still, choosing N4 is sufficient and direct.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN9 -> N12, N1\nN10 -> N13, N4\nN3 -> N5, N7\nN4 -> N13, N0\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6, N9\nN11 -> terminal\nN2 -> N11, N10\nN5 -> N2, N8\nN13 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N1\n\nLegal moves: N2, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N2 and N8. N8 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N8 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "epi