lly terminate, meaning the player who moves to N7 will lose if the opponent plays optimally.  \nTherefore, choosing N3 guarantees a win. Hence, the best move is to N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N3, N7\nN4 -> N5, N9\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN3 -> N1\nN2 -> N5, N3\nN7 -> N4, N0\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the only legal move is to N1, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N1 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N1 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4939728353140917, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the only legal move is to N1, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N1 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N1 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N11\n\nDirected graph:\nN12 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N8, N3, N6, N5\nN10 -> N12\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N10\nN11 -> N2, N7, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN2 -> N1\nN1 -> N6, N4, N9\nN7 -> N0\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N13, N7\n\nLegal moves: N2, N7, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N11, the legal moves are to N2, N7, or N8.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N10, then to N12 (terminal). So the opponent wins if we move to N8.  \n- Moving to N7 leads to N0, which is terminal. So we move to a terminal and win immediately.  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N1, from which the opponent can go to N9 (terminal), or to N4 or N6. But from N6, the opponent can go to N7 and then to N0, which is terminal.  \n  However, moving to N7 leads directly to terminal, which means the current player (us) wins if we take that path.  \nThus, choosing N7 leads to a terminal node in the next move — so we win. This is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.9395302773061687, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N11, the legal moves are to N2, N7, or N8.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N10, then to N12 (terminal). So the opponent wins if we move to N8.  \n- Moving to N7 leads to N0, which is terminal. So we move to a terminal and win immediately.  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N1, from which the opponent can go to N9 (terminal), or to N4 or N6. But from N6, the opponent can go to N7 and then to N0, which is terminal.  \n  However, moving to N7 leads directly to terminal, which means the current player (us) wins if we take that path.  \nThus, choosing N7 leads to a terminal node in the next move — so we win. This is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your 