[2026-08-12 14:57:48] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N5, N6\nN2 -> N4, N7\nN7 -> N3, N9\nN4 -> N0, N8\nN0 -> N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N4 and N7.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N0 or N8.  \n  - N0 → N1 (terminal), so opponent wins.  \n  - N8 → N5 or N6; N5 → N0 or N9 (N9 terminal), N6 → terminal. So, either way opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N3 or N9; both lead to terminal nodes immediately. So the opponent loses immediately.  \nThus, choosing N7 forces a win. Therefore, the optimal move is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5603565365025467, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N4 and N7.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N0 or N8.  \n  - N0 → N1 (terminal), so opponent wins.  \n  - N8 → N5 or N6; N5 → N0 or N9 (N9 terminal), N6 → terminal. So, either way opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N3 or N9; both lead to terminal nodes immediately. So the opponent loses immediately.  \nThus, choosing N7 forces a win. Therefore, the optimal move is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N5, N6\nN2 -> N4, N7\nN7 -> N3, N9\nN4 -> N0, N8\nN0 -> N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N3 and N9. N3 and N9 both lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, the player to move from N7 wins by choosing either N3 or N9. Since both options end the game immediately with a win, either is optimal. However, to maximize the outcome, choosing N9 is equally valid as N3. But as the question asks to choose one legal destination that maximizes the outcome, and both lead to immediate win, either is correct. We select N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4430390492359932, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N3 and N9. N3 and N9 both lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, the player to move from N7 wins by choosing either N3 or N9. Since both options end the game immediately with a win, either is optimal. However, to maximize the outcome, choosing N9 is equally valid as N3. But as the question asks to choose one legal destination that maximizes the outcome, and both lead to immediate win, either is correct. We select N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N3, N0\nN7 -> N5\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N9\nN8 -> N9, N1, N4\nN1 -> N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N1, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N9, N1, and N4.  \n- N9 leads to N2, then to N3 (terminal), N7, or N0.  \n  - N3 → terminal → win for the opponent if we move here.  \n  - N7 → N5 → terminal → opponent loses, so this is a winning move.  \n- N1 → N6 → terminal → opponent loses, so this is a winning move.  \n- N4 → N2 or N9.  \n  - N2 → N7 → N5 → terminal or N3 or N0, all terminal.  \n  \nAll paths from N9 and N4 eventually lead to terminal nodes or via N7 to N5.  \nThe key is N1 → N6 → terminal. The opponent has no move. So, choosing N1 immediately leads to a terminal state for the opponent, winning the game.  \nThus, N1 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.29069043576683656, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N9, N1, and N4.  \n- N9 leads to N2, then to N3 (terminal), N7, or N0.  \n  - N3 → terminal → win for the opponent if we move here.  \n  - N7 → N5 → terminal → opponent loses, so this is a winning move.  \n- N1 → N6 → terminal → opponent loses, so this is a winning move.  \n- N4 → N2 or N9.  \n  - N2 → N7 → N5 → terminal or N3 or N0, all terminal.  \n  \nAll paths from N9 and N4 eventually lead to terminal nodes or via N7 to N5.  \nThe key is N1 → N6 → terminal. The opponent has no move. So, choosing N1 immediately leads to a terminal state for the opponent, winning the game.  \nThus, N1 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N3, N0\nN7 -> N5\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N2, N9\nN8 -> N9, N1, N4\nN1 -> N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N1, the only legal move is to N6, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N6 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N6 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4939728353140917, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N1, the only legal move is to N6, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N6 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N6 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N0, N3\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N4, N2, N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN4 -> N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N0, N5\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9\nN2 -> N7, N8\n\nLegal moves: N4, N2, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N4, N2, and N8. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position for the player who moves.<br>• Moving to N4: next is N1 (to N0 o