 final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N0, N6\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N1, N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9\nN9 -> terminal\nN0 -> N3\nN5 -> N8, N7, N2\nN7 -> N1, N4\n\nLegal moves: N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, the only legal move is to N9, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N9 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N9 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4888794567062818, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, the only legal move is to N9, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N9 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N9 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N7, N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN7 -> N4, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N0, N5\nN6 -> N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N8\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N6, N2\n\nLegal moves: N0, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N1, the legal moves are to N0 and N5.  \n- Moving to N0: leads to N6 or N2.  \n  - From N6: to N3 (terminal) → opponent wins.  \n  - From N2: to N7 or N8.  \n    - N7 → N4 (terminal) or N6 (→ N3).  \n    - N8 → terminal.  \n  So from N0, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N9 or N8.  \n  - Both N9 and N8 are terminal. So the opponent has no move.  \nThus, moving to N5 forces the opponent into a terminal state immediately. This is a winning move.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5926146010186757, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N1, the legal moves are to N0 and N5.  \n- Moving to N0: leads to N6 or N2.  \n  - From N6: to N3 (terminal) → opponent wins.  \n  - From N2: to N7 or N8.  \n    - N7 → N4 (terminal) or N6 (→ N3).  \n    - N8 → terminal.  \n  So from N0, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N9 or N8.  \n  - Both N9 and N8 are terminal. So the opponent has no move.  \nThus, moving to N5 forces the opponent into a terminal state immediately. This is a winning move.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N7, N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN7 -> N4, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N0, N5\nN6 -> N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N8\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N6, N2\n\nLegal moves: N9, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9 and N8. N9 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<