5 leads to a forced win for the current player.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN6 -> N4\nN7 -> N1, N5\nN2 -> N4, N9\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N3\nN3 -> N5, N8\nN5 -> N0, N6\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N0 and N6. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N0 and N6. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N4\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> N3, N2\nN6 -> N4, N0, N1\nN5 -> N8, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\n