ition.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N7 or N8.  \n  - N7 is terminal.  \n  - N8 leads to N1 (terminal).  \nThus, from N9, all moves lead to terminal for the opponent. So the current player (us) wins by moving to N9.  \nTherefore, choosing N9 is optimal as it leads to the opponent having no move or forcing them to lose.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N6, N8\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N9\nN6 -> N2, N3\nN8 -> N1\nN9 -> N7, N8\nN2 -> N5, N3\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N7 and N8. N7 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N7 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N7 and N8. N7 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N7 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not outp