[2026-08-12 15:29:06] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N6, N0, N2\nN0 -> N2, N4\nN3 -> N5, N9, N4\nN9 -> N1\nN8 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7\nN4 -> N8\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N9, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5, N9, and N4. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N7 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N1. From N1, the opponent can move to N6, N0, or N2—all of which eventually lead to terminal nodes. Thus, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N8 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and loses.  \nThus, moving to N4 is a winning move because it ends the game immediately for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N4 maximizes our outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.26097906055461245, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5, N9, and N4. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N7 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N1. From N1, the opponent can move to N6, N0, or N2—all of which eventually lead to terminal nodes. Thus, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N8 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and loses.  \nThus, moving to N4 is a winning move because it ends the game immediately for the opponent. Therefore, choosing N4 maximizes our outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N6, N0, N2\nN0 -> N2, N4\nN3 -> N5, N9, N4\nN9 -> N1\nN8 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7\nN4 -> N8\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the only legal move is to N8, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N8 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N8 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4888794567062818, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the only legal move is to N8, which leads to terminal. Thus, the player who moves to N8 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Therefore, moving to N8 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. No other choice exists, so this is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N3, N4\nN4 -> N7, N5\nN8 -> N0, N9\nN6 -> N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6, N8\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N7\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N3 and N4.  \n- Moving to N3: leads to N6 or N8.  \n  - From N6: to N1 (terminal, opponent wins).  \n  - From N8: to N0 or N9.  \n    - N0 → terminal.  \n    - N9 → N4 or N7.  \n      - N4 → N7 or N5 (both eventually terminal).  \n      - N7 → terminal.  \n    So from N3, the opponent can be forced into a terminal state.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N7 or N5.  \n  - Both N7 and N5 go directly to terminal. So the opponent has no move and loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N4 immediately ends the game with the opponent having no legal move. Therefore, choosing N4 is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6112903225806452, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N3 and N4.  \n- Moving to N3: leads to N6 or N8.  \n  - From N6: to N1 (terminal, opponent wins).  \n  - From N8: to N0 or N9.  \n    - N0 → terminal.  \n    - N9 → N4 or N7.  \n      - N4 → N7 or N5 (both eventually terminal).  \n      - N7 → terminal.  \n    So from N3, the opponent can be forced into a terminal state.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N7 or N5.  \n  - Both N7 and N5 go directly to terminal. So the opponent has no move and loses immediately.  \n\nThus, moving to N4 immediately ends the game with the opponent having no legal move. Therefore, choosing N4 is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinki