 terminal or N7 (terminal).  \n    - From N3: to terminal.  \nThus, moving to N2 gives the current player control over a winning path. The optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N4\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N9, N5\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0, N7\nN1 -> N0, N8\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N2\n\nLegal moves: N9, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N9 and N5.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N4 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N1 or N3.  \n  - From N1: to N0 (terminal) or N8.  \n    - N8 → N0 or N7 (N7 terminal).  \n    - So from N5, the opponent can go to N3 (terminal) or N1 → N8 → N0 or N7 (all terminal).  \n  - Thus, moving to N5 gives the current player a winning strategy.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 0.42351443123938876, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N9 and N5.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N4 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N1 or N3.  \n  - From N1: to N0 (terminal) or N8.  \n    - N8 → N0 or N7 (N7 terminal).  \n    - So from N5, the opponent can go to N3 (terminal) or N1 → N8 → N0 or N7 (all terminal).  \n  - Thus, moving to N5 gives the current player a winning strategy.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}]
