[2026-08-12 15:40:02] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N3, N4, N7\nN2 -> N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6\nN3 -> N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N5\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN1 -> N3, N2, N0\n\nLegal moves: N3, N2, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N1, the legal moves are to N3, N2, and N0. We analyze each destination to determine the optimal move to maximize the chance of winning.  \n- N3 → N9 (terminal): The opponent wins immediately.  \n- N2 → N8 → N6 (terminal): The opponent wins after one move.  \n- N0 → N4 or N5.  \n  - N4 → terminal: opponent wins.  \n  - N5 → N3, N4, N7.  \n    - N3 → N9 (terminal), N4 → terminal, N7 → terminal. All lead to terminal.  \nThus, from N0, any move leads to terminal. So, N0 leads to the opponent having no move.  \nThus, choosing N0 forces the opponent to a losing position. Therefore, N0 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.27116581777023213, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N1, the legal moves are to N3, N2, and N0. We analyze each destination to determine the optimal move to maximize the chance of winning.  \n- N3 → N9 (terminal): The opponent wins immediately.  \n- N2 → N8 → N6 (terminal): The opponent wins after one move.  \n- N0 → N4 or N5.  \n  - N4 → terminal: opponent wins.  \n  - N5 → N3, N4, N7.  \n    - N3 → N9 (terminal), N4 → terminal, N7 → terminal. All lead to terminal.  \nThus, from N0, any move leads to terminal. So, N0 leads to the opponent having no move.  \nThus, choosing N0 forces the opponent to a losing position. Therefore, N0 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N3, N4, N7\nN2 -> N8\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6\nN3 -> N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N5\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN1 -> N3, N2, N0\n\nLegal moves: N4, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N4 and N5. N4 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N4 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N4 and N5. N4 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N4 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N4 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N2\nN3 -> N8\nN6 -> N4, N5, N3\nN2 -> N1, N7, N3\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN7 -> N9\nN5 -> N4\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N5, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N4, N5, and N3. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position for the player who moves there (assuming optimal play).  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N0 or N2. N0 and N1 are terminal. N2 leads to N1, N7, or N3. N1 and N3 lead to terminal or N8 (terminal). N7 leads to N9 (terminal). So from N2, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 (then N0 or N2). N0 and N2 are terminal or lead to terminal. This results in a losing position for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N3: leads to N8 (terminal). So the opponent has no move, wins immediately.  \nThus, moving to N4 gives the player more control over the game. The analysis shows N4 leads to a win.  \nTherefore, choosing N4 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.30087719298245624, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N4, N5, and N3. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position for the player who moves there (assuming optimal play).  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N0 or N2. N0 and N1 are terminal. N2 leads to N1, N7, or N3. N1 and N3 lead to terminal or N8 (terminal). N7 leads to N9 (terminal). So from N2, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N4 (then N0 or N2). N0 and N2 are terminal or lead to terminal. This results in a losing position for the opponent.  \n- Moving to N3: leads to N8 (terminal). So the opponent has no move, wins immediately.  \nThus, moving to N4 gives the player more control over the game. The analysis shows N4 leads to a win.  \nTherefore, choosing N4 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N5\nN6 -> N3, N0\nN3 -> N1, N8\nN9 -> N2, N4\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N7\nN2 -> N6, N8\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N2 and N4.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N6 or N8.  \n  - From N6: to N3 or N0 (N0 is terminal, so N3 is better).  \n    - From N3: to N1 or N8 (both terminal or lead to N8).  \n    - From N8: to N5 (terminal).  \n  - So from N2, the opponent can eventually be forced to a terminal state.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N5 or N7 (both terminal).  \n  - Immediate loss.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 gives the current player a winning strategy. The optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4175721561969439, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N2 and N4.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N6 or N8.  \n  - From N6: to N3 or N0 (N0 is terminal, so N3 is better).  \n    - From N3: to N1 or N8 (both terminal or lead to N8).  \n    - From N8: to N5 (terminal).  \n  - So from N2, the opponent can eventually be forced to a terminal state.  \n- Moving to N4: leads to N5 or N7 (both terminal).  \n  - Immediate loss.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 gives the current player a winning strategy. The optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A respo