ing move.  \n- N7 → N9 (terminal) or N5 (leads to N3, N4, N2). All lead to terminal or forced loss. So N7 leads to opponent having options, but all result in terminal states or forced wins. But N5 → N2 → N3 is terminal. So N7 allows opponent to win via N5.  \nTherefore, N6 leads directly to terminal (N8), and the opponent has no move. This is a winning move.  \nThus, moving to N6 maximizes our outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N8\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N0, N6, N7\nN2 -> N3\nN7 -> N9, N5\nN5 -> N3, N4, N2\n\nLegal moves: N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N8. N8 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N8 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. Therefore, choosing N8 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 0.49057724957555177, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N8. N8 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N8 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N8 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. Therefore, choosing N8 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}]
