rected graph:\nN7 -> N13\nN11 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN10 -> N2, N0\nN2 -> N12\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N5, N9\nN3 -> N6, N10, N0\nN6 -> N8\nN5 -> N2, N1, N11\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N7, N4, N13\n\nLegal moves: N6, N10, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N6, N10, and N0.  \n- N6 → N8 (terminal) → immediate win for the player who moves to N8.  \n- N10 → N2 or N0.  \n  - N2 → N12 (terminal) or N1 → N7, N4, N13 (all terminal).  \n  - N0 → N5 or N9 (N9 terminal, N5 → N2, N1, N11 — all terminal).  \n- N0 → N5 or N9 (N9 terminal, N5 → N2 → terminal or N1 → terminal).  \n\nAll paths from N10 or N0 eventually lead to terminal nodes. But from N6, we go directly to N8 (terminal), so the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N6 results in an immediate win if it's your turn.  \nTherefore, moving to N6 maximizes the outcome.  \n</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.2966327108092814, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N6, N10, and N0.  \n- N6 → N8 (terminal) → immediate win for the player who moves to N8.  \n- N10 → N2 or N0.  \n  - N2 → N12 (terminal) or N1 → N7, N4, N13 (all terminal).  \n  - N0 → N5 or N9 (N9 terminal, N5 → N2, N1, N11 — all terminal).  \n- N0 → N5 or N9 (N9 terminal, N5 → N2 → terminal or N1 → terminal).  \n\nAll paths from N10 or N0 eventually lead to terminal nodes. But from N6, we go directly to N8 (terminal), so the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N6 results in an immediate win if it's your turn.  \nTherefore, moving to N6 maximizes the outcome.  \n</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not o