inal, N8 leads to N0 or N1. N0 leads to N5 (terminal), N1 is terminal.  \n  - Thus, from N9, the opponent is forced into a terminal or losing position.  \nThus, moving to N9 gives the current player a winning strategy.  \nTherefore, choosing N9 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4235144312393888, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N2 and N9.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N6 or N1. N6 and N1 are terminal, so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N7 or N2.  \n  - From N7: to N8 or N3. N3 is terminal, N8 leads to N0 or N1. N0 leads to N5 (terminal), N1 is terminal.  \n  - Thus, from N9, the opponent is forced into a terminal or losing position.  \nThus, moving to N9 gives the current player a winning strategy.  \nTherefore, choosing N9 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N0, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8, N3\nN0 -> N5\nN9 -> N7, N2\nN4 -> N2, N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N1\n\nLegal moves: N7, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N7 and N2.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N8 or N3.  \n  - From N8: to N0 or N1 (N1 ends the game, N0 → N5 → terminal).  \n  - From N3: terminal.  \n  So from N7, the opponent can be forced into a terminal or losing position.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N6 or N1.  \n  - Both N6 and N1 are terminal.  \nThus, moving to N7 gives the current player a winning strategy because it leads to a position where the opponent has limited or losing options.  \nTherefore, choosing N7 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4192699490662139, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N7 and N2.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N8 or N3.  \n  - From N8: to N0 or N1 (N1 ends the game, N0 → N5 → terminal).  \n  - From N3: terminal.  \n  So from N7, the opponent can be forced into a terminal or losing position.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N6 or N1.  \n  - Both N6 and N1 are terminal.  \nThus, moving to N7 gives the current player a winning strategy because it leads to a position where the opponent has limited or losing options.  \nTherefore, choosing N7 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N0, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8, N3\nN0 -> N5\nN9 -> N7, N2\nN4 -> N2, N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N1\n\nLegal moves: N8, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N8 and N3. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N3 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N8 and N3. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N3 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N3, N5\nN7 -> N6, N2\nN2 -> N8, N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N4\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7, N2\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N3 and N5.  \n- Moving to N3: leads to N1 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N7 or N2.  \n  - From N7: to N6 (terminal) or N2.  \n    - N6 is terminal (opponent wins).  \n    - N2: to N8 or N9 (both terminal).  \n  - Thus, from N5, the player can force a win by moving to N2, then to N8 or N9 (both terminal).  \nTherefore, moving to N5 is optimal because it leads to a winning position.  \nThe best choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4201188455008489, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N3 and N5.  \n- Moving to N3: leads to N1 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N7 or N2.  \n  - From N7: to N6 (terminal) or N2.  \n    - N6 is terminal (opponent wins).  \n    - N2: to N8 or N9 (both terminal).  \n  - Thus, from N5, the player can force a win by moving to N2, then to N8 or N9 (both terminal).  \nTherefore, moving to N5 is optimal because it leads to a winning position.  \nThe best choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N3, N5\nN7 -> N6, N2\nN2 -> N8, N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N4\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7, N2\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N7 and N2.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N6 or N2.  \n  - N6 leads to terminal (win for the opponent if it's their turn).  \n  - N2 leads to N8 or N9.  \n    - N8 → N9 or N4 (both terminal).  \n    - N9 → terminal.  \n    - N4 → terminal.  \n  So from N7, the opponent can force a win if we go to N6. But if we go to N2, the opponent is in a position where all moves lead to terminal.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 or N9, both of which eventually end in terminal.  \n  So the opponent has no legal moves after we go to N2.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 leads to a terminal position for the opponent — meaning we win.  \nTherefore, choosing N2 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.3759762308998302, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N7 and N2.  \n- Moving to N7: leads to N6 or N2.  \n  - N6 leads to terminal (win for the opponent if it's their turn).  \n  - N2 leads to N8 or N9.  \n    - N8 → N9 or N4 (both terminal).  \n    - N9 → terminal.  \n    - N4 → terminal.  \n  So from N7, the opponent can force a win if we go to N6. But if we go to N2, the opponent is in a position where all moves lead to terminal.  \n- Moving to N2: leads to N8 or N9, both of which eventually end in terminal.  \n  So the opponent has no legal moves after we go to N2.  \n\nThus, moving to N2 leads to a terminal position for the opponent — meaning we win.  \nTherefore, choosing N2 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N3, N5\nN7 -> N6, N2\nN2 -> N8, N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N4\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7, N2\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N8, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N8 and N9. N9 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N8 and N9. N9 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}]
