[2026-08-12 15:54:28] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N0\nN6 -> N4, N7, N1\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> N9, N4\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9\nN9 -> N3, N5, N2\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N7, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N4, N7, and N1.  \n- N7 leads to N0, which ends in terminal. The player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move).  \n- N4 leads to N9. From N9, the opponent can go to N3 (terminal), N5, or N2 (both terminal). So from N9, the opponent can force a win by moving to N5 or N2.  \n- N1 leads to N9 or N4. Again, both N9 and N4 lead to positions where the opponent can eventually force a win.  \n\nThus, moving to N7 leads directly to N0 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and loses. This is a winning move.  \nTherefore, choosing N7 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.26607243916242224, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N4, N7, and N1.  \n- N7 leads to N0, which ends in terminal. The player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move).  \n- N4 leads to N9. From N9, the opponent can go to N3 (terminal), N5, or N2 (both terminal). So from N9, the opponent can force a win by moving to N5 or N2.  \n- N1 leads to N9 or N4. Again, both N9 and N4 lead to positions where the opponent can eventually force a win.  \n\nThus, moving to N7 leads directly to N0 (terminal), so the oppon