[2026-08-12 15:56:59] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> terminal\nN11 -> N6, N10\nN1 -> N8, N5\nN9 -> N12, N7\nN13 -> N6, N11\nN3 -> N12, N10\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N13\nN12 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN8 -> N3, N9\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N4\n\nLegal moves: N8, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N1, the legal moves are to N8 and N5.  \n- Moving to N8: leads to N3 or N9.  \n  - From N3: to N12 (terminal) or N10 (terminal).  \n  - From N9: to N12 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  Both result in terminal nodes, so the opponent wins if we go to N8.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N0 or N4.  \n  - From N0: to N2 (terminal) or N13.  \n    - From N13: to N6 (terminal) or N11.  \n      - From N11: to N6 (terminal) or N10 (terminal).  \n  Thus, from N5, we can reach N13 and eventually force the opponent into a terminal node.  \nThus, moving to N5 leads to a winning position.  \nTherefore, choosing N5 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6299660441426147, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N1, the legal moves are to N8 and N5.  \n- Moving to N8: leads to N3 or N9.  \n  - From N3: to N12 (terminal) or N10 (terminal).  \n  - From N9: to N12 (terminal) or N7 (terminal).  \n  Both result in terminal nodes, so the opponent wins if we go to N8.  \n- Moving to N5: leads to N0 or N4.  \n  - From N0: to N2 (terminal) or N13.  \n    - From N13: to N6 (terminal) or N11.  \n      - From N11: to N6 (ter