[2026-08-12 16:06:23] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N4\nN9 -> N5, N2\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5, N9\nN6 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7, N0\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N1, N8\nN8 -> N6\n\nLegal moves: N9, N1, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9, N1, and N8.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N5 or N2. N2 ends the game (win for the opponent if they move next), N5 leads to N7 or N0 (both eventually terminal). N7 → N4 (terminal), N0 → terminal. So from N9, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N1: leads to N5 or N9. N5 → N7 or N0 (both terminal), N9 → N5 or N2 (same as above). All paths eventually end. So opponent wins if we go to N1.  \n- Moving to N8: leads to N6 (terminal). The opponent has no move, so they lose. This is a winning move.  \nThus, moving to N8 leads to an immediate terminal state for the opponent, so it is optimal. The best choice is N8.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.2889926428975666, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9, N1, and N8.  \n- Moving to N9: leads to N5 or N2. N2 ends the game (win for the opponent if they move next), N5 leads to N7 or N0 (both eventually terminal). N7 → N4 (terminal), N0 → terminal. So from N9, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N1: leads to N5 or N9. N5 → N7 or N0 (both terminal), N9 → N5 or N2 (same as above). All paths eventually end. So opponent wins if we go to N1.  \n- Moving to N8: leads to N6