[2026-08-12 16:21:55] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N6, N5, N8\nN1 -> N0\nN9 -> N3, N1\nN5 -> N4\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N5\nN6 -> N9, N2\nN0 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N6, N5, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N6, N5, and N8.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N4 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N9 or N2.  \n  - From N9: to N3 or N1.  \n    - N3 and N1 lead to terminal or N0 (terminal).  \n  - From N2: terminal.  \n  So from N6, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N6 or N5.  \n  - N5 → N4 (terminal).  \n  - N6 → N9 or N2 (same as above).  \nThus, moving to N6 gives the current player a winning strategy because it leads to a position where the opponent has a losing move.  \nTherefore, choosing N6 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.2779569892473119, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N6, N5, and N8.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N4 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N9 or N2.  \n  - From N9: to N3 or N1.  \n    - N3 and N1 lead to terminal or N0 (terminal).  \n  - From N2: terminal.  \n  So from N6, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N6 or N5.  \n  - N5 → N4 (terminal).  \n  - N6 → N9 or N2 (same as above).  \nThus, moving to N6 gives the current player a winning strategy because it leads to a position where the opponent has a losing move.  \nTherefore, choosing N6 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N6, N5, N8\nN1 -> N0\nN9 -> N3, N1\nN5 -> N4\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N5\nN6 -> N9, N2\nN0 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N9 and N2. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N9 and N2. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N3, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N0\nN1 -> N2, N5\nN3 