[2026-08-12 16:23:10] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N12\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N13, N10\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N8, N1\nN7 -> N11, N0\nN5 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N7\nN3 -> terminal\nN11 -> N5, N0\nN13 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> N3, N10\nN4 -> N2, N6\nN12 -> N4, N8\n\nLegal moves: N4, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N12, the legal moves are to N4 and N8.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N2 or N6.  \n  - N2 → terminal (win for the opponent).  \n  - N6 → N8 or N1.  \n    - N8 → N9 or N7.  \n      - N9 → N13 or N10 (both terminal).  \n      - N7 → N11 or N0 (both terminal).  \n    - N1 → N3 or N10 (both terminal).  \n  So from N4, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N9 or N7.  \n  - N9 → N13 or N10 (terminal).  \n  - N7 → N11 or N0 (terminal).  \nThus, moving to N4 gives the current player a winning strategy because it leads to a position where the opponent has no non-terminal moves.  \nTherefore, choosing N4 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6359083191850594, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N12, the legal moves are to N4 and N8.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N2 or N6.  \n  - N2 → terminal (win for the opponent).  \n  - N6 → N8 or N1.  \n    - N8 → N9 or N7.  \n      - N9 → N13 or N10 (both terminal).  \n      - N7 → N11 or N0 (both terminal).  \n    - N1 → N3 or N10 (both terminal).  \n  So from N4, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N9 or N7.  \n  - N9 → N13 or N10 (terminal).  \n  - N7 → N11 or N0 (terminal).  \nThus, moving to N4 gives the current player a winning strategy because it leads to a position where the opponent has no non-terminal moves.  \nTherefore, choosing N4 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N13, N10\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N8, N1\nN7 -> N11, N0\nN5 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N7\nN3 -> terminal\nN11 -> N5, N0\nN13 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> N3, N10\nN4 -> N2, N6\nN12 -> N4, N8\n\nLegal moves: N2, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N2 and N6. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N2 and N6. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<