[2026-08-12 16:25:47] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N2\nN5 -> N3, N9, N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N1\nN0 -> N9, N1, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> N0\nN9 -> N4, N7\n\nLegal moves: N3, N9, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N3, N9, and N8.  \n- N3 leads to N2 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- N9 leads to N4 (terminal) or N7. N7 leads to N1 (terminal), so from N9, the opponent can only move to terminal. Thus, N9 is a winning move.  \n- N8 leads to N0. From N0, the opponent can move to N9, N1, or N6. N1 and N6 are terminal, but N9 leads to N4 or N7 (both terminal). So from N0, the opponent can force a win. Thus, N8 leads to a winning position for the opponent.  \nThus, moving to N9 leads to a terminal state for the opponent, so it is a winning move. Therefore, choosing N9 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.2788058856819469, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N3, N9, and N8.  \n- N3 leads to N2 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- N9 leads to N4 (terminal) or N7. N7 leads to N1 (terminal), so from N9, the opponent can only move to terminal. Thus, N9 is a winning move.  \n- N8 leads to N0. From N0, the opponent can move to N9, N1, or N6. N1 and N6 are terminal, but N9 leads to N4 or N7 (both terminal). So from N0, the opponent can force a win. Thus, N8 leads to a winning position for the oppo