[2026-08-12 16:44:48] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N9\nN1 -> N6, N9\nN3 -> terminal\nN7 -> N0, N8\nN0 -> N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N2, N4\nN4 -> N5, N3\nN6 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N0 and N8.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N1, then to N6 or N9. N6 and N9 are terminal, so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N2 or N4. N2 is terminal, so the opponent wins. N4 leads to N5 or N3. N5 leads to N0 or N9 (N9 is terminal, N0 leads to N1, then to N6 or N9). Thus, from N4, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \nThus, moving to N8 allows the current player to force a win by going to N4, then to N5, then to N0 or N9 (both eventually terminal).  \nTherefore, choosing N8 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5994057724957556, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N0 and N8.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N1, then to N6 or N9. N6 and N9 are terminal, so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N2 or N4. N2 is terminal, so the opponent wins. N4 leads to N5 or N3. N5 leads to N0 or N9 (N9 is terminal, N0 leads to N1, then to N6 or N9). Thus, from N4, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \nThus, moving to N8 allows the current player to force a win by going to N4, then to N5, then to N0 or N9 (both eventually terminal).  \nTherefore, choosing N8 is optimal.</re