: "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N2, N9, and N0.  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N7, then to N5 (terminal), so the opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N8 (terminal) or N1 or N2.  \n  - N8 is terminal (opponent wins immediately).  \n  - N1 leads to N4 or N0.  \n    - N4 is terminal.  \n    - N0 leads to N3 (terminal).  \n  - So from N9, the player can move to N1, then to N0 or N4 (both terminal), giving the opponent no move. Thus, from N9, the current player can force a win.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N3 (terminal), so the opponent wins.  \nThus, moving to N9 is the only winning move. The optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.2813525749858518, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N2, N9, and N0.  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N7, then to N5 (terminal), so the opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N8 (terminal) or N1 or N2.  \n  - N8 is terminal (opponent wins immediately).  \n  - N1 leads to N4 or N0.  \n    - N4 is terminal.  \n    - N0 leads to N3 (terminal).  \n  - So from N9, the player can move to N1, then to N0 or N4 (both terminal), giving the opponent no move. Thus, from N9, the current player can force a win.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N3 (terminal), so the opponent wins.  \nThus, moving to N9 is the only winning move. The optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN1 -> N4, N0\nN7 -> N5\nN6 -> N2, N9, N0\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> N8, N1, N2\nN0 -> N3\nN2 -> N7\nN3 -> terminal