[2026-08-12 16:59:34] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N6, N5\nN1 -> N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2, N8\nN4 -> N0, N1\nN7 -> N2, N9\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> N3, N1\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N0 and N1.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N6 or N5. N5 is terminal (win for the opponent if they move), N6 leads to N3 or N1. N3 leads to N2 (terminal) or N8 (terminal); N1 leads to N2 or N9 (both terminal). So from N0, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N2 or N9, both terminal. The opponent immediately wins.  \nThus, moving to N0 gives the current player a chance to force a win. Therefore, choosing N0 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5696943972835314, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N0 and N1.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N6 or N5. N5 is terminal (win for the opponent if they move), N6 leads to N3 or N1. N3 leads to N2 (terminal) or N8 (terminal); N1 leads to N2 or N9 (both terminal). So from N0, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N2 or N9, both terminal. The opponent immediately wins.  \nThus, moving to N0 gives the current player a chance to force a win. Therefore, choosing N0 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N6, N5\nN1 -> N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2, N8\nN4 -> N0, N1\nN7 -> N2, N9\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> N3, N1\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N6, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N6 and N5. N5 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N6 and N5. N5 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N7, N2\nN8 -> N5, N3\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7\nN6 -> N8, N0\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> N6, N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9, N6\n\nLegal moves: N9, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 and N6.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N6 or N1.  \n  - From N6, the opponent can move to N8 or N0 (both eventually terminal or lead to terminal).  \n  - From N1, the opponent can move to N7 (terminal) or N2 (terminal).  \n  So from N9, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - N8 → N5 or N3 (N3 is terminal, N5 → N7 (terminal)).  \n  - N0 is terminal.  \n  So from N6, all moves lead to terminal nodes. The player who moves to N6 wins immediately because the opponent has no move after that.  \nThus, moving to N6 is a winning move.  \nTherefore, choosing N6 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.61553480475382, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 and N6.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N6 or N1.  \n  - From N6, the opponent can move to N8 or N0 (both eventually terminal or lead to terminal).  \n  - From N1, the opponent can move to N7 (terminal) or N2 (terminal).  \n  So from N9, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N8 or N0.  \n  - N8 → N5 or N3 (N3 is terminal, N5 → N7 (terminal)).  \n  - N0 is terminal.  \n  So from N6, all moves lead to terminal nodes. The player who moves to N6 wins immediately because the opponent has no move after that.  \nThus, moving to N6 is a winning move.  \nTherefore, choosing N6 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N7, N2\nN8 -> N5, N3\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N7\nN6 -> N8, N0\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> N6, N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN4 -> N9, N6\n\nLegal moves: N8, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N8 and N0. N0 leads 