 node.  \nThus, moving to N6 leads to a winning position. Therefore, choosing N6 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N11, N13\nN3 -> N9, N10\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN10 -> N4, N0\nN9 -> N7, N8\nN11 -> terminal\nN6 -> N1, N2\nN4 -> N13, N11\nN12 -> N10, N6\nN7 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN2 -> N5, N3\n\nLegal moves: N1, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N1 and N2. N1 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N1 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N1 and N2. N1 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N1 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N2, N1