[2026-08-12 17:14:32] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N6\nN4 -> N2, N1\nN3 -> N9, N5\nN0 -> N7\nN8 -> N0, N4, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N3, N6\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N4, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N0, N4, and N3.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N7, then to N3 or N6. N3 leads to N9 (terminal) or N5 (then N6); N6 is terminal. So from N7, the opponent can win if we go to N7.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N2 or N1, both terminal. So opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9 (terminal) or N5 (then N6, terminal). So the opponent has no move if we go to N3.  \n\nThus, moving to N3 leads to a win for the current player.  \nTherefore, choosing N3 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.25333899264289766, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N8, the legal moves are to N0, N4, and N3.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N7, then to N3 or N6. N3 leads to N9 (terminal) or N5 (then N6); N6 is terminal. So from N7, the opponent can win if we go to N7.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N2 or N1, both terminal. So opponent wins.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9 (terminal) or N5 (then N6, terminal). So the opponent has no move if we go to N3.  \n\nThus, moving to N3 leads to a win for the current player.  \nTherefore, choosing N3 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> N6\nN4 -> N2, N1\nN3 -> N9, N5\nN0 -> N7\nN8 -> N0, N4, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N3, N6\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9 and N5. N9 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9 and N5. N9 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N9, N5\nN9 -> N4, N3\nN8 -> N6, N1\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N8, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N8 and N5.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N6 or N1. N1 is terminal (win for the opponent), N6 leads to N9 or N5. N9 → N4 (terminal) or N3 (terminal); N5 → N9 or N2. N2 → N0 (terminal). So from N8, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N9 or N2. N9 → N4 or N3 (terminal); N2 → N0 (terminal). Both are terminal. So from N5, the opponent has no move after that. Thus, moving to N5 results in an immediate win for the current player.  \nThus, choosing N5 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4056876061120542, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N8 and N5.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N6 or N1. N1 is terminal (win for the opponent), N6 leads to N9 or N5. N9 → N4 (terminal) or N3 (terminal); N5 → N9 or N2. N2 → N0 (terminal). So from N8, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N9 or N2. N9 → N4 or N3 (terminal); N2 → N0 (terminal). Both are terminal. So from N5, the opponent has no move after that. Thus, moving to N5 results in an immediate win for the current player.  \nThus, choosing N5 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N9, N5\nN9 -> N4, N3\nN8 -> N6, N1\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N9, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9 and N2. Moving to N2 leads to N0 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately. Moving to N9 leads to N4 or N3, both of which are terminal. Thus, from N9, the opponent has no move and loses. Therefore, moving to N9 is a winning move. Thus, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.47784380305602714, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N9 and N2. Moving to N2 leads to N0 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately. Moving to N9 leads to N4 or N3, both of which are terminal. Thus, from N9, the opponent has no move and loses. Therefore, moving to N9 is a winning move. Thus, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> N9, N5\nN9 -> N4, N3\nN8 -> N6, N1\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N4, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N4 and N3. N4 and N3 both lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves result in an immediate win for the current player. Since either move leads to a win, both are optimal. However, choosing either is equivalent because both lead to terminal states. But since the problem asks to choose one, and both are valid, we select one. N3 is a direct terminal, so it's a winning move. Thus, moving to N3 is valid and optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.44388794567062817, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N9, the legal moves are to N4 and N3. N4 and N3 both lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves result in