rom N6, the player can go to N11 → N1, then the opponent loses.  \nTherefore, choosing N6 leads to a winning strategy.  \nThus, the optimal move is to N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> N7\nN8 -> N13, N9\nN4 -> N5\nN1 -> N4, N12\nN13 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> N8, N9\nN2 -> N0, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN5 -> N10\nN11 -> N13, N1\nN12 -> N3\nN6 -> N10, N11\nN7 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N10, N11assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N10 and N11. N10 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N10 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N10 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N10.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4931239388794566, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N10 and N11. N10 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N10 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N10 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N10.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N5, N3, N1\nN5 -> N6, N4\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN9 -> N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N6, N5\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0\nN3 -> N9\n\nLegal moves: N5, N3, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N5, N3, or N1.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N6 (terminal) or N4 (then to N0, terminal). So the opponent wins if we go to N5.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9, then to N8 (terminal). So the opponent has no move after we go to N3. This is a winning move.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N2 (terminal), N6 (terminal), or N5 (then to N6 or N4). All paths eventually end. The opponent wins.  \nThus, moving to N3 is the only winning move. The optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 1.7551499717034522, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N5, N3, or N1.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N6 (terminal) or N4 (then to N0, terminal). So the opponent wins if we go to N5.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9, then to N8 (terminal). So the opponent has no move after we go to N3. This is a winning move.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N2 (terminal), N6 (terminal), or N5 (then to N6 or N4). All paths eventually end. The opponent wins.  \nThus, moving to N3 is the only winning move. The optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N5, N3, N1\nN5 -> N6, N4\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN9 -> N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N6, N5\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0\nN3 -> N9\n\nLegal moves: N9assistan