he outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N2\nN0 -> N1, N4\nN7 -> N0, N8\nN4 -> N2\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N4, N3\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N5, N9\n\nLegal moves: N1, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N1 and N4.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N6 or N2. N2 is terminal (win for the opponent if they move), N6 leads to N5 or N9 (both terminal). So from N1, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N2 (terminal). So the current player wins immediately.  \nThus, moving to N4 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4591680814940577, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N1 and N4.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N6 or N2. N2 is terminal (win for the opponent if they move), N6 leads to N5 or N9 (both terminal). So from N1, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N2 (terminal). So the current player wins immediately.  \nThus, moving to N4 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N2\nN0 -> N1, N4\nN7 -> N0, N8\nN4 -> N2\nN3 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N4, N3\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N5, N9\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N2 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.49142614601018675, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately because the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N2 is the only option, and it results in an immediate win for the current player. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N9, N8\nN2 -> N5, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N8\nN3 -> N6\nN8 -> N9, N2\n\nLegal moves: N7, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N7 and N8.  \n- Moving to N7 leads to N9 or N8.  \n  - From N9: to N0 (terminal) or N1 (terminal). Both are terminal.  \n  - From N8: to N9 or N2.  \n    - N9 → N0 or N1 (terminal).  \n    - N2 → N5 or N3.  \n      - N5 → terminal.  \n      - N3 → N6 (terminal).  \n  So from N7, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N9 or N2.  \n  - N9 → N0 or N1 (terminal).  \n  - N2 → N5 or N3 (both eventually terminal).  \nThus, from N4, moving to N7 gives the current player a winning strategy. Therefore, choosing N7 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6214770797962649, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N7 and N8.  \n- Moving to N7 leads to N9 or N8.  \n  - From N9: to N0 (terminal) or N1 (terminal). Both are terminal.  \n  - From N8: to N9 or N2.  \n    - N9 → N0 or N1 (terminal).  \n    - N2 → N5 or N3.  \n      - N5 → terminal.  \n      - N3 → N6 (terminal).  \n  So from N7, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N9 or N2.  \n  - N9 → N0 or N1 (terminal).  \n  - N2 → N5 or N3 (both eventually terminal).  \nThus, from N4, moving to N7 gives the current player a winning strategy. Therefore, choosing N7 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N9, N8\nN2 -> N5, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N8\nN3 -> N6\nN8 -> N9, N2\n\nLegal moves: N9, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N7, the legal moves are to N9 and N8.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N0 or N1. N0 and N1 are terminal, so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N9 or N2.  \n  - From N9, the opponent can go to N0 or N1 (terminal).  \n  - From N2, the opponent can go to N5 or N3. N5 is te