[2026-08-12 17:31:51] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N0, N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N2\nN6 -> N5\nN4 -> N8, N6\nN8 -> N9, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N1, N9\n\nLegal moves: N8, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N8 and N6.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N9 or N3. N9 is terminal (win for the opponent), N3 leads to N0 or N7. N0 is terminal, N7 leads to N1 or N9 (both terminal). So from N8, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N5. From N5, the opponent can go to N0 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). Both are terminal. So the opponent loses.  \nThus, moving to N6 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4320033955857385, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N8 and N6.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N9 or N3. N9 is terminal (win for the opponent), N3 leads to N0 or N7. N0 is terminal, N7 leads to N1 or N9 (both terminal). So from N8, the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N5. From N5, the opponent can go to N0 (terminal) or N2 (terminal). Both are terminal. So the opponent loses.  \nThus, moving to N6 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N0, N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N2\nN6 -> N5\nN4 -> N8, N6\nN8 -> N9, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N1, N9\n\nLegal moves: N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N5. From N5, the player can move to N0 or N2. N0 and N2 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 from N6 allows the opponent to be forced into a terminal node. Therefore, moving to N5 is the only option, and it leads to a winning position. Thus, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4625636672325976, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the only legal move is to N5. From N5, the player can move to N0 or N2. N0 and N2 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to them wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N5 from N6 allows the opponent to be forced into a terminal node. Therefore, moving to N5 is the only option, and it leads to a winning position. Thus, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N0, N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N2\nN6 -> N5\nN4 -> N8, N6\nN8 -> N9, N3\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N1, N9\n\nLegal moves: N0, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N0 and N2. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.49906621392190154, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N0 and N2. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> N1, N4\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N6\nN3 -> N5, N1, N9\nN6 -> N2\nN0 -> N7, N9\n\nLegal moves: N5, N1, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N5, N1, and N9.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N8 (terminal), so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N1 or N4; N1 leads to N8 (terminal), N4 is terminal. So the opponent can force a win.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N0 or N6.  \n  - From N0: to N7 (terminal) or N9 (then to N1 or N4, both terminal).  \n  - From N6: to N2 (terminal).  \nThus, from N5, the opponent has no winning move regardless. So moving to N5 is a winning move.  \nThus, choosing N5 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 1.7424165251839274, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, 