nswer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N9, N0\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N1\nN9 -> N8, N5\nN7 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N1\nN2 -> N9, N6\nN6 -> N3, N4\nN1 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N3 and N4.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N7 or N1. N7 and N1 are terminal, so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N9 or N0. N0 is terminal, but N9 leads to N8 or N5. N8 leads to N1 (terminal), N5 is terminal. So from N9, the opponent can move to N8 or N5 (both terminal). Thus, from N4, the opponent has no winning move.  \nThus, moving to N4 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.4320033955857385, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N3 and N4.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N7 or N1. N7 and N1 are terminal, so the opponent wins immediately.  \n- Moving to N4 leads to N9 or N0. N0 is terminal, but N9 leads to N8 or N5. N8 leads to N1 (terminal), N5 is terminal. So from N9, the opponent can move to N8 or N5 (both terminal). Thus, from N4, the opponent has no winning move.  \nThus, moving to N4 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N4.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N9, N0\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> N7, N1\nN9 -> N8, N5\nN7 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N1\nN2 -> N9, N6\nN6 -> N3, N4\nN1 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 and N0. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N4, the legal moves are to N9 and N0. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6\nN0 -> N9, N7\nN9 -> N8, N2\nN8 -> N3, N4\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N5\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N1, N4\n\nLegal moves: N9, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N9 and N7.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N8 or N2.  \n  - From N8: to N3 (terminal) or N4 (terminal).  \n  - From N2: to N7 or N5.  \n    - N5 is terminal.  \n    - N7 leads to N1 or N4.  \n      - N1 → N6 (terminal).  \n      - N4 → terminal.  \n  So from N9, the op