[2026-08-12 17:57:10] [agentic_pipeline.py (513)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 508552] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N0, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N8\nN3 -> N9, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7, N0\nN6 -> N3, N2\nN9 -> N4\n\nLegal moves: N3, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N3 and N2.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9 or N1. N9 → N4 (terminal), N1 → terminal. So from N3, the opponent can move to N4 or N1 (both terminal), meaning the player who moves to N3 wins if the opponent has no choice.  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N7 or N8. N7 → N0 or N5 (both terminal), N8 → N7 or N0 (both terminal). All resulting nodes lead to terminal states. So from N2, all moves lead to terminal nodes. Thus, the player who moves to N2 loses.  \nThus, moving to N3 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.5909168081494058, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N6, the legal moves are to N3 and N2.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9 or N1. N9 → N4 (terminal), N1 → terminal. So from N3, the opponent can move to N4 or N1 (both terminal), meaning the player who moves to N3 wins if the opponent has no choice.  \n- Moving to N2 leads to N7 or N8. N7 → N0 or N5 (both terminal), N8 → N7 or N0 (both terminal). All resulting nodes lead to terminal states. So from N2, all moves lead to terminal nodes. Thus, the player who moves to N2 loses.  \nThus, moving to N3 is a winning move. The optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> N0, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN2 -> N7, N8\nN3 -> N9, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7, N0\nN6 -> N3, N2\nN9 -> N4\n\nLegal moves: N9, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9 and N1. N1 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N1 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 1.4990662139219015, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N3, the legal moves are to N9 and N1. N1 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N1 wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, moving to N1 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN2 -> N1\nN6 -> N9, N2\nN3 -> N7, N5\nN8 -> N2, N3\nN7 -> N5, N4\nN0 -> N6, N8\n\nLegal moves: N6, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N6 and N8.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N9 or N2. N9 and N2 lead to terminal nodes, so the opponent wins immediately if we go to N6.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N2 or N3.  \n  - From N2: to N1 (terminal).  \n  - From N3: to N7 or N5. N7 → N5 or N4 (both terminal), N5 → terminal.  \nThus, from N8, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \nTherefore, moving to N8 allows the current player to force a win.  \nThus, choosing N8 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": 1.419269949066214, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N0, the legal moves are to N6 and N8.  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N9 or N2. N9 and N2 lead to terminal nodes, so the opponent wins immediately if we go to N6.  \n- Moving to N8 leads to N2 or N3.  \n  - From N2: to N1 (terminal).  \n  - From N3: to N7 or N5. N7 → N5 or N4 (both terminal), N5 → terminal.  \nThus, from N8, the opponent can be forced into a terminal node.  \nTherefore, moving to N8 allows the current player to force a win.  \nThus, choosing N8 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> N3\nN0 -> N7, N1, N9\nN3 -> N2\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N4\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> N8, N3\nN5 -> N0, N6, N8\n\nLegal moves: N0, N6, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N5, the legal moves are to N0, N6, and N8.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N7, N1, or N9. N1 and N9 are terminal (win for the opponent if they move), N7 leads to N4 (terminal). So from N0, the opponent can fo